<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>SEPA structured addresses</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Schemes & Rules</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">SEPA structured addresses</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>SEPA structured address rules</strong> are set by the EPC rulebooks for SCT, SCT Inst, SDD and OCT Inst. <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> has been mandatory in EPC SCT since November 2025; <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> becomes mandatory at the November 2026 cutover, from which only structured and hybrid formats are allowed in both the Customer-to-PSP and Inter-PSP spaces.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How SEPA structured addresses works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>A payer address is required at all only when either PSP sits in a non-EEA SEPA country; intra-EEA it is optional. The cutover applies at 03h30 CET for SCT Inst and OCT Inst. The governing guidance is EPC 153-22, which also records the alignment of the cutover date to 15 November 2026.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §6.5, §10.5–§10.6 (Table 24), Appendix H.1–H.2; EPC 153-22 v2.1; EPC 153-22 v2.1 (Oct 2025).</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
